  "definition": {
   "definition": "CPI measures the average change over time in retail prices of a fixed basket of goods and services consumed by households. All-India CPI for Rural, Urban and Combined is compiled and released monthly (with a one-month lag) by the National Statistical Office, MoSPI; the Combined series (CPI-C) is the headline retail-inflation measure used for RBI's flexible inflation-targeting framework. The base year was revised from 2012=100 to 2024=100 by MoSPI (weights drawn from the Household Consumption Expenditure Survey 2023-24; 358 weighted items; COICOP 2018 classification). The dashboard computes y-o-y inflation from the 2024=100 Combined index.",
